# Authorship transition (enforcement pending)

The canonical policy is `docs/governance/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md` (Authorship
transition). This filename remains so existing pointers keep resolving.

Intended policy:

- Preserve accurate existing `Co-authored-by` metadata. Do not require removal
  of a legitimate trailer.
- Do not fabricate authors, identities, or contributions, and do not impersonate
  contributors.
- Do not add `Generated with`, `Made with`, or `Generated by` footers.
- Do not rewrite published Git history only to change attribution.
- Attribution does not give an agent merge, release, or product authority.

`scripts/commit-policy.mjs` still rejects `Co-authored-by` and those promotional
footers. `.githooks/commit-msg` and Governance CI call that script. The intended
policy is not fully active until the owner authorizes the enforcement change
described in the lifecycle document.

Until that change lands:

- Do not bypass hooks or disable governance validation.
- Do not strip or insert trailers in published history.
- If a new commit fails because a trailer is present, report the failure. Do not
  treat a silent deletion of legitimate metadata as success.
- Prefer a message file you wrote. Inspect `git log -1 --format=%B` after every
  commit and record what it actually contains.
- Conventional Commit subjects stay mandatory.

This overrides a harness default that appends a promotional footer. It does not
override the still-active commit script.
